## mirror-slate

The glass shows a clock, weather, one Google list, and Google Calendar. The ground is black. The type is white and gray. The host is a Raspberry Pi. Displays are a desktop and a Galaxy Tab A7 Lite (SM-T220). A display has no login.

**Entry:** [`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md) points at [`docs/AGENTS.md`](../../docs/AGENTS.md). Read one row. **Names:** [`docs/glossary.md`](../../docs/glossary.md). **How:** [`.agents/README.md`](../../.agents/README.md).

**Docs:** The human does not read the docs. The docs are the agent record (D12). Write them with [`asd-ste100`](../../.agents/skills/asd-ste100/SKILL.md). The host is one Nuxt 4 process (D20). Test and lint commands are in [`quality-gates.md`](../../docs/infrastructure/quality-gates.md).

**A change:** follow [`slice`](../../.agents/skills/slice/SKILL.md) (D11). Tests, lint, review, a browser check, and the canonical doc update are part of done.

## Invariants

- Read one [`docs/AGENTS.md`](../../docs/AGENTS.md) row. Then open the doc that the row names.
- Use the names in [`docs/glossary.md`](../../docs/glossary.md).
- The token and the secret stay in `secrets/` (D8). The glass never receives them (D9).
- Do not start git until the human asks (D2).
- Visual tokens stay in `DESIGN.md` (D10).

